Manage context

Usage:
  bootwright context [command]

Available Commands:
  current     Show the current context
  delete      Permanently delete a context and its local files
  init        Initialize a configured context and select it
  list        List contexts
  update      Update Context configuration or Environment input
  use         Select the current context

Global Flags:
      --context string             Select a context (default: current context)
  -h, --help                       Show help for this command
      --ssh-ask-sudo-password      Request the borrowed account's sudo password
      --ssh-id-file string         Offer an explicit private key for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user string            Borrow an explicit POSIX account for eligible SSH access
      --ssh-user-for-provisioned   Extend the borrowed account to provisioned machines

Use "bootwright context [command] --help" for more information about a command.
